-- Phase 5: one-time existing-hospital credential/identity regeneration.
-- Generated from phase5_dryrun_report.csv, reviewed and approved by the user
-- before this file was written. Updates h_code/name/username/password IN
-- PLACE for 147 real hospitals (2 taluka-gap + 8 test-looking rows excluded,
-- see the plan doc) - no rows deleted. Passwords are bcrypt-hashed with
-- Python's bcrypt lib ($2b$, cost 12) - verified compatible with Spring
-- Security's BCryptPasswordEncoder/PasswordCompat (accepts $2a$/$2b$/$2y$,
-- see PasswordCompat's own BCRYPT_PATTERN). must_change_password is set so
-- every affected hospital is prompted to change it after first login with
-- the new credentials, same convention as any newly-created account.
-- NOT idempotent by design (re-running would re-hash already-new passwords
-- and re-derive already-new usernames off the NEW names, corrupting them) -
-- run exactly once against local SQLEXPRESS nrc_live.

